# Default: git stores LF, checks out native. `core.autocrlf=true` already does
# this locally; committing it makes the behaviour survive a fresh clone.
* text=auto

# Wire captures are BYTES, not text. The game stream uses bare LF, and
# `no_fixture_has_carriage_returns_or_is_empty` asserts these files carry no
# CR. Letting autocrlf convert them on checkout turns that test red on a clean
# clone -- which is exactly how it failed mid-session on 2026-09-18 when a
# `git stash -u` round-trip rewrote them as CRLF.
crates/cena-protocol/tests/fixtures/*.xml -text

# The crit tables are data the loader parses line by line, and a golden digest
# is taken over the parsed result. Keep them byte-stable across platforms.
crates/cena-model/data/*.tsv -text

# Upstream map scripts kept VERBATIM: the converter matches them byte for byte
# (`recognise/routines.rs`), and upstream writes them with bare LF. A checkout
# that turned those into CRLF would silently un-port every exit that uses one.
# The same for the converter's fixture, which is a cut of the upstream file.
crates/cena-mapdb-convert/src/upstream_scripts/* -text
crates/cena-mapdb-convert/tests/fixtures/*.json -text
